-- title:
--   Idelic unit index of an order localises at one place
-- statement:
--   Let $a,b\in\mathbb{Q}$ and let $\Lambda$ be a $\mathbb{Z}$-submodule of the quaternion algebra $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]$ which is an order in the sense of the project predicate [`QuaternionAlgebra.IsOrder`](def/QuaternionAlgebra_Order.html#L11): $1\in\Lambda$, $\Lambda$ is closed under multiplication, its $\mathbb{Q}$-span is all of $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]$, and it is finitely generated. Let $v$ be a height-one prime of $\mathcal{O}_{\mathbb{Q}}=\mathbb{Z}$ and let $s$ be a unit of $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]\otimes_{\mathbb{Q}}\mathbb{A}^{f}$, where $\mathbb{A}^{f}$ denotes the finite adele ring. For a height-one prime $w$ write $\Lambda_w$ for [`Submodule.localBox Λ w`](def/Submodule_LocalBox.html#L40), the additive subgroup of $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]\otimes_{\mathbb{Q}}\mathbb{Q}_w$ generated by the elements $z\otimes c$ with $z\in\Lambda$ and $c$ in the valuation ring of the completion at $w$, write $\Lambda_w^{\times}$ for the stabiliser of the underlying set of $\Lambda_w$ in $(\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]\otimes_{\mathbb{Q}}\mathbb{Q}_w)^{\times}$ under the pointwise multiplication action, and write $s_w$ for the image of $s$ under the unit map induced by [`Submodule.finiteAdeleEvalAt`](def/Submodule_LocalBox.html#L36) at $w$. Assume that for every $w\neq v$ and every $u\in\Lambda_w^{\times}$ one has $s_w^{-1}us_w\in\Lambda_w^{\times}$. Let $\widehat{\Lambda}^{\times}$ be [`Submodule.finiteIdeleStabilizer Λ`](def/Submodule_FiniteAdeleBox.html#L26), the stabiliser in $(\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]\otimes_{\mathbb{Q}}\mathbb{A}^{f})^{\times}$ of the additive subgroup generated by the elements $z\otimes\alpha$ with $z\in\Lambda$ and $\alpha$ a finite adele all of whose components are integral. Then the relative index of $\widehat{\Lambda}^{\times}\cap s\widehat{\Lambda}^{\times}s^{-1}$ in $\widehat{\Lambda}^{\times}$ equals the relative index of $\Lambda_v^{\times}\cap s_v\Lambda_v^{\times}s_v^{-1}$ in $\Lambda_v^{\times}$, as natural numbers (the value $0$ recording an infinite index), the conjugates being taken as images under the inner automorphisms associated with $s$ and with $s_v$.
--
--   This localises, at the single place $v$, the index of the unit group of an order against a conjugate of it by a finite idele — the quantity that measures the number of one-sided cosets in a double coset $\widehat{\Lambda}^{\times}s\widehat{\Lambda}^{\times}$, hence the degree of the associated Hecke-type correspondence. It is used in the Čerednik–Drinfeld part of the development, in the computation of relative indices for elements of the level and prime Hecke sets attached to an intersection of an order with a conjugate.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_QuaternionAlgebra_IsOrder_relIndex_finiteIdeleStabilizer_inf_map_conj_eq_local.lean

